module.exports = "STD 6 TENSE QUIZ (20 MARKS)\n\nQ1. Which of the following sentences is in the simple present tense?\nA) She is playing the piano.\nB) They walk to school every day.\nC) He will visit his grandmother tomorrow.\nD) I ate an apple.\n\nQ2. Identify the verb in the simple past tense in this sentence: \"The dog barked at the stranger.\"\nA) The\nB) barked\nC) stranger\nD) dog\n\nQ3. Choose the correct simple future tense form to complete the sentence: \"We ________ to the zoo next Sunday.\"\nA) will go\nB) went\nC) goes\nD) are going\n\nQ4. Which sentence is written in the present continuous tense?\nA) Mother cooks dinner.\nB) Mother cooked dinner.\nC) Mother is cooking dinner.\nD) Mother will cook dinner.\n\nQ5. Complete the sentence with the correct past continuous form: \"When I entered the room, the children ________.\"\nA) sleep\nB) were sleeping\n*C) slept\nD) are sleeping\n\nQ6. Fill in the blank with the correct simple present form: \"The sun ________ in the east.\"\nA) rise\nB) rose\nC) rises\nD) is rising\n\nQ7. What is the simple past tense of the irregular verb \"write\"?\nA) written\nB) writing\nC) writes\nD) wrote\n\nQ8. Identify the correct present continuous form for the pronoun \"I\" and verb \"read\".\nA) I am reading\nB) I is reading\nC) I are reading\nD) I readed\n\nQ9. Which of the following sentences is in the past continuous tense?\nA) They played football in the rain.\nB) They are playing football in the rain.\nC) They were playing football in the rain.\nD) They will play football in the rain.\n\nQ10. Which word tells you that a sentence is in the simple future tense?\nA) did\nB) will\nC) is\n*D) was\n\nQ11. Choose the correct form: \"My friends ________ football every evening.\"\nA) plays\nB) played\nC) play\nD) playing\n\nQ12. Convert this sentence into the simple past tense: \"She sings a sweet song.\"\nA) She sang a sweet song.\nB) She sings a sweet song.\nC) She will sing a sweet song.\nD) She is singing a sweet song.\n\nQ13. When do we use the present continuous tense (am/is/are + verb-ing)?\nA) For actions happening right now at the moment of speaking\nB) For habits that happened yesterday\nC) For permanent universal truths\nD) For actions completed long ago\n\nQ14. Fill in the blank: \"At 8 o'clock last night, it ________ heavily.\"\nA) rains\nB) is raining\nC) rained\nD) was raining\n\nQ15. Complete the sentence: \"I hope you ________ pass the exam.\"\nA) will\nB) did\nC) do\nD) are\n\nQ16. Identify the sentence that shows correct subject-verb agreement in the simple present tense.\nA) The cat catch mice.\nB) The boys reads a book.\nC) The baby cries at night.\nD) Birds flies high.\n\nQ17. What is missing in this present continuous sentence? \"He ________ watching TV.\"\nA) am\nB) are\nC) is\nD) be\n\nQ18. What is the simple past tense of the irregular verb \"go\"?\nA) goed\nB) went\nC) gone\nD) going\n\nQ19. Which sentence refers to an action that will happen in the future?\nA) I cleaned my room.\nB) I am cleaning my room.\nC) I clean my room.\nD) I will clean my room tomorrow.\n\nQ20. Which helping verbs are used to form the past continuous tense?\nA) is / are\nB) do / does\n*C) will / shall\nD) was / were\n\nANSWER KEY:\n1. B\n2. B\n3. A\n4. C\n5. B\n6. C\n7. D\n8. A\n9. C\n10. B\n11. C\n12. A\n13. A\n14. D\n15. A\n16. C\n17. C\n18. B\n19. D\n20. D\n";
